# Naming Conventions

## Folders

- `kebab-case`, all lowercase.
- Examples: `user-profile`, `auth`, `settings`

## Hooks

- `camelCase`, must start with `use`.
- Examples: `useAuth.ts`, `useUserSettings.ts`

## Components

- `PascalCase`; filename matches exported component name.
- Examples: `LoginForm.tsx`, `UserCard.tsx`

## Schemas (Zod)

- `camelCase`, suffix `Schema`.
- Examples: `userSchema.ts`, `paymentMethodSchema.ts`

## Services

- `camelCase`; suffix `Service` or `Api`.
- Examples: `authService.ts`, `userApi.ts`

## Server actions

- File: `actions.ts` per feature module (see `next-architecture.mdc`).

## Tests

- Same base name + `.test.tsx` or `.spec.ts`.
- Examples: `LoginForm.test.tsx`, `authService.spec.ts`

## Next.js App Router files

- Use framework names as-is: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `route.ts`.
